.TH tkudialog n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkudialog
.PP
Dialogs whose \fBmessage text is selectable and copyable\fR (Ctrl\-C or the Copy button) \-\- unlike \fBtk_messageBox\fR. A generic, extensible builder plus ready\-made variants. Pure Tk; no tclutils engine required.
.SS "Generic / extensible"
.CS
# non-modal toplevel (embed or drive yourself)
::tkutils::tkudialog::build  $win ?-title t? ?-message m? ?-icon info|warning|error|question? \
                                 ?-detail d? ?-buttons {labels...}? ?-entry 0|1? ?-initial s? \
                                 ?-parent w?
# modal: builds, grabs, waits, returns the clicked button label
::tkutils::tkudialog::show    $win ?same options?
::tkutils::tkudialog::getText $win          ;# message text
::tkutils::tkudialog::getDetail $win
::tkutils::tkudialog::result  $win
::tkutils::tkudialog::copyText $win          ;# copies message (+detail), returns it
::tkutils::tkudialog::choose  $win label     ;# pick a button programmatically
.CE
.SS "Ready\-made variants"
.CS
::tkutils::tkudialog::showInfo    message ?options?   ;# returns OK
::tkutils::tkudialog::showWarning message ?options?
::tkutils::tkudialog::showError   message ?-detail d?
::tkutils::tkudialog::confirm     message ?options?   ;# 1 for Yes, else 0
::tkutils::tkudialog::input       ?-title t? ?-message m? ?-initial s? ?-parent w?   ;# entered text or ""
.CE
.PP
Extend by passing your own \fB\-buttons\fR and \fB\-detail\fR, or build a non\-modal dialog with \fBbuild\fR and wire it up yourself. The ready\-made variants pass any further options (such as \fB\-parent\fR) through to \fBshow\fR.
.SS "Parent and placement (0.2)"
.PP
\fB\-parent w\fR makes the dialog belong to the toplevel of \fBw\fR: it is transient to it and opens centred over it. Without \fB\-parent\fR the parent is the toplevel that has the keyboard focus, else \fB.\fR — as with \fBtk_messageBox\fR. Pass \fB\-parent\fR whenever the calling window is known; it is the only reliable answer on a machine with several monitors.
.PP
Up to 0.1 \fB\-parent\fR was accepted but not used: no \fBwm transient\fR, and every modal dialog opened in the middle of the screen (measured 2026\-09\-19: parent at 900,600, dialog at 431,466). With the application on a second monitor, the dialog appeared on the other one.
.PP
Details of the placement:
.IP \(bu
The dialog is made transient only to a \fBviewable\fR parent — a dialog transient to a withdrawn toplevel stays invisible under some window managers.
.IP \(bu
A \fB\-parent\fR that does not exist is an error, \fB{TKUTILS TKUDIALOG PARENT <w>}\fR.
.IP \(bu
The dialog is kept on the screen (all four sides) only when the parent lies completely on the screen Tk reports. \fBTk reports one screen\fR: on Windows that is the primary monitor, so a parent on a second monitor lies outside it. Clamping there would pull the dialog back to the primary monitor, so it is centred over the parent without clamping; a dialog wider than its parent may then overhang that monitor. The rule is \fB_geometry\fR and is tested for this case with made\-up coordinates — two real monitors were not measured.
.SS "Options are checked (0.2)"
.PP
An unknown option is an error that lists the known ones, with \fB{TKUTILS TKUDIALOG OPTION <opt>}\fR:
.CS
unknown option "-parnet"
Known: -title -message -icon -detail -buttons -entry -initial -parent
.CE
.PP
Up to 0.1 \fBarray set\fR swallowed it — \fBbuild .d \-parnet .p\fR built the dialog without a parent, and \fBform\fR with a typo opened and waited as if nothing were wrong.
.SS Launcher
.CS
tclsh bin/tkudialog.tcl
.CE
.SS "Form dialog"
.CS
set vals [::tkutils::tkudialog::form $fieldspec ?-title T? ?-parent w?]
# -> values dict on OK, "" on Cancel
.CE
.PP
Embeds a \fBtkutils::tkuform\fR (see docs/tkuform.md) in a modal dialog with OK/Cancel. Example:
.CS
set v [::tkutils::tkudialog::form {
    {name title label "Title" type entry}
    {name prio  label "Prio"  type combo values {low normal high} default normal}
    {name done  label "Done"  type check}
} -title "New note"]
if {$v ne ""} { puts "title=[dict get $v title]" }
.CE
